            ENDF/B-VII.1 EVALUATION MODIFICATIONS                 9222 1451   12
                             2/27/2011                            9222 1451   13
      P.G.Young, P.Talou, T. Kawano, M.B.Chadwick, (LANL)         9222 1451   14
                                                                  9222 1451   15
                  ----- SUMMARY -----                             9222 1451   16
                                                                  9222 1451   17
   The ENDF/B-VII.1 evaluation is a modification of the ENDF/B-   9222 1451   18
VII.0 evaluation to correct the cross sections and angular        9222 1451   19
distributions of the ground-state rotational band of 233U, i.e.,  9222 1451   20
MF=3,4, MT=51,52,53,55,58,65. The correction was required because 9222 1451   21
the compound-nucleus components for these states in the Version   9222 1451   22
VIII.0 evaluation did not take proper account of fission          9222 1451   23
competition. In addition, the inelastic cross section below 1 MeV 9222 1451   24
exhibited an anomalous peak, mainly due to MT=51,52.  The         9222 1451   25
following changes were made:                                      9222 1451   26
                                                                  9222 1451   27
1. The compound nucleus cross sections for MT=51,52,53,55,58,65   9222 1451   28
were re-calculated and combined with the direct components from   9222 1451   29
ECIS calculations.                                                9222 1451   30
2. The MF=4, MT=53,55,58,65 data were replaced with these         9222 1451   31
data.                                                             9222 1451   32
3. The MF=3, MT=53,55,58,65 data were also replaced with these    9222 1451   33
data.                                                             9222 1451   34
4. The corrected results for MF=3,4, MT=51,52 were found to       9222 1451   35
inadequately reproduce the measurements of Haouat et. al (Ha82    9222 1451   36
below). It was surmised that the deformed optical model potential 9222 1451   37
used in the evaluation might not be adequate at incident energies 9222 1451   38
below approximately 1.0-1.5 MeV. Therefore, to correct this       9222 1451   39
problem, the compound nucleus contributions to these states were  9222 1451   40
scaled by a single factor to produce better agreement with the    9222 1451   41
Haouat et al. experiment.  The difference in the inelastic cross  9222 1451   42
section was absorbed in the elastic cross section.                9222 1451   43
5. The data were modified for MF=3,4, MT=2,51,52 (the MT=2        9222 1451   44
change was small).                                                9222 1451   45
                                                                  9222 1451   46
