    L. Leal, H. Derrien, Guber, N. Larson, R. Wright,             9222 1451   58
                    R.Spencer (ORNL)                              9222 1451   59
                                                                  9222 1451   60
                  ----- SUMMARY -----                             9222 1451   61
   The ENDF/B-VII evaluation is a complete revision of almost all 9222 1451   62
the data in the 233U evaluation. Major features of the evaluation 9222 1451   63
are:                                                              9222 1451   64
1. A new evaluation of the (n,f) cross section based on ENDF/B-   9222 1451   65
   VII standard cross section analysis is incorporated.           9222 1451   66
2. A new evaluation of nubar consistent with experimental data    9222 1451   67
   within uncertainties and with fast critical benchmark          9222 1451   68
   measurements is included.                                      9222 1451   69
3. New resolved and unresolved resonance parameter data are       9222 1451   70
   incorporated.                                                  9222 1451   71
4. Improved delayed neutron data are incorporated.                9222 1451   72
5. Coupled-channels optical model calculations are used to        9222 1451   73
   provide scattering cross sections and angular distributions.   9222 1451   74
6. New reaction theory calculations are utilized for (n,xn) and   9222 1451   75
   other reactions.                                               9222 1451   76
7. Compound nucleus and direct reaction cross sections and        9222 1451   77
   angular distributions are extended to an excitation energy of  9222 1451   78
   1.5 MeV.                                                       9222 1451   79
8. Fission neutron spectra from JENDL-3.3 are adopted.            9222 1451   80
9. Covariance matrix evaluations for all energy ranges.           9222 1451   81
                                                                  9222 1451   82
            ----- DETAILED DESCRIPTION -----                      9222 1451   83
                                                                  9222 1451   84
>> MF=1 GENERAL INFORMATION                                       9222 1451   85
                                                                  9222 1451   86
MT=452: TOTAL AVERAGE NEUTRON MULTIPLICITY PER FISSION (TOTAL     9222 1451   87
        NUBAR)                                                    9222 1451   88
   Sum of MT=455 and 456. Adopted the ENDF/B-VII thermal standard 9222 1451   89
value of 2.4968.                                                  9222 1451   90
                                                                  9222 1451   91
MT=455: AVERAGE DELAYED NEUTRON MULTIPLICITY PER FISSION          9222 1451   92
   Based on new delayed neutron 6-group parameters from CINDER'90 9222 1451   93
summation calculations.  The CINDER calculations (Wi05) are based 9222 1451   94
on a new CINDER library in which beta-decay half-lives and beta-  9222 1451   95
delayed neutron-emission probablities are obtained from the       9222 1451   96
evaluated experimental data file NuBase2003 (Au03), when          9222 1451   97
available there. When experimental data are not available, the    9222 1451   98
data are calculated in a model where allowed Gamow-Teller decays  9222 1451   99
are treated in a microscopic quasi-particle random-phase          9222 1451  100
approximation (QRPA) and the first forbidden decays are treated   9222 1451  101
in the statistical gross theory (Mo03). (typo fixed by TK 2009)   9222 1451  102
                                                                  9222 1451  103
MT=456: AVERAGE PROMPT NEUTRON MULTIPLICITY PER FISSION           9222 1451  104
    1.e-5 eV - 10 eV: Adopted the thermal value of 2.4894 for     9222 1451  105
prompt nubar, corresponding to the ENDF/B-VII thermal standard    9222 1451  106
value of 2.4968 for total nubar.                                  9222 1451  107
    10 eV - 30 MeV: Generally based on results from the           9222 1451  108
covariance analysis of experimental data performed for ENDF/B-VI, 9222 1451  109
after correction for the ENDF/B-VII standard 252Cf nubar value.   9222 1451  110
We attempted to follow the covariance data as well as possible    9222 1451  111
but mainly to stay within uncertainties in the data and to keep   9222 1451  112
good agreement with fast critical benchmarks.                     9222 1451  113
