>> MF=5 ENERGY DISTRIBUTIONS OF SECONDARY PARTICLES               9222 1451  395
                                                                  9222 1451  396
MT=18: Prompt Fission Neutron Spectrum Matrix                     9222 1451  397
   The MT=18 spectra are taken from the JENDL-3.3 evaluation      9222 1451  398
(Ma02). That evaluation utilizes a modified form (Oh92) of the    9222 1451  399
Madland and Nix Los Alamos model (MN82). The compound nucleus     9222 1451  400
formation cross sections for fission fragments (FF) were          9222 1451  401
calculated using Becchetti-Greenlees potential (Be69).  Up to     9222 1451  402
4th-chance-fission were considered at high incident neuttron      9222 1451  403
energies.  The Ignatyuk formula (Ig79) were used to generate the  9222 1451  404
level density parameters.                                         9222 1451  405
Parameters adopted:                                               9222 1451  406
     Total average FF kinetic energy = 172.311-0.0212*E(MeV)      9222 1451  407
     Average energy release          = 188.438 MeV                9222 1451  408
     Average mass number of light FF =  95                        9222 1451  409
     Average mass number of heavy FF = 139                        9222 1451  410
     Level density of the light FF   =  9.999- 10.094             9222 1451  411
     Level density of the heavy FF   = 11.89 - 12.20              9222 1451  412
Note that the parameters vary with the incident energy within the 9222 1451  413
indicated range.                                                  9222 1451  414
                                                                  9222 1451  415
MT=455: DELAYED NEUTRON EMISSION SPECTRA FROM FISSION             9222 1451  416
   The abundances are based on the new delayed-neutron            9222 1451  417
calculations (Wi05) described under MF=1, MT=455. However, the    9222 1451  418
earlier six-group spectra from ENDF/B-VI are carried over to      9222 1451  419
ENDF/B-VII because new multigroup spectra have not yet been       9222 1451  420
calculated with the new library.                                  9222 1451  421
                                                                  9222 1451  422
